TESTSUITE "INTCALC"

*> INTCALC is the daily interest-accrual batch. It walks every open
*> interest-bearing account (SAV/MMA/CDA/IRA) via INT_CURSOR, calls the
*> INTRATE assembler routine to compute one day's interest on the
*> current balance, accrues it into the account, and -- only on that
*> account's statement-cycle day -- pays the accrued interest out as a
*> posted transaction and resets the accrual to zero. Every account also
*> gets a BANK.DAILY_BALANCE snapshot row. These cases exercise: the
*> cursor-open failure abort, the fetch dispatch (hit/exhausted/fatal
*> DB2 error), the accrue-only vs. pay-day branches, a zero-balance
*> edge case, the INTRATE and DB2-update error paths, the interest
*> posting sub-paragraph on its own (success and insert-failure), a
*> multi-account run across three product tiers, and the finalize
*> return-code logic.
*>
*> NOTE ON TEST SHAPE: 0000-MAIN-PROCESS and 1000-INITIALIZE's own
*> STOP RUN cannot be exercised through the top-level entry point in
*> this suite -- see the "THRU 2200-EXIT" note below for why -- so every
*> case here targets the specific paragraph whose logic it is verifying,
*> the same style used by examples/real-world/DEPTMQP/DEPTMQP.cut.

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 1000-INITIALIZE
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

TESTCASE "1000-INITIALIZE opens the report file and the interest cursor"
    MOCK OPEN INTRPT
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "OPEN"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 1000-INITIALIZE
    VERIFY OPEN INTRPT WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED 2 TIMES
    VERIFY SQL "OPEN" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> If INT_CURSOR can't open (e.g. DB2 subsystem down), the batch must
*> abort immediately with RC 16 rather than attempt to process accounts
*> against a cursor that was never opened.
TESTCASE "1000-INITIALIZE aborts with RC 16 when the interest cursor fails to open"
    MOCK OPEN INTRPT
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "OPEN"
        MOVE -805 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 1000-INITIALIZE
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 16
    VERIFY SQL "OPEN" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT (cursor dispatch)
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

TESTCASE "2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT calculates interest for a fetched account"
    MOCK SQL "FETCH"
        MOVE "HV000000001" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
        MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
        MOVE 15000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
        MOVE 2.500000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
        MOVE 10.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
        MOVE 200.00 TO HV-INTEREST-YTD
        MOVE "20" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 08 TO WS-CURRENT-DAY
    PERFORM 2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT
    EXPECT WS-ACCTS-PROCESSED TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 1
    VERIFY CALL "INTRATE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> WHEN +100: the cursor is exhausted -- CONTINUE, no account is
*> touched.
TESTCASE "2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT does nothing once the cursor is exhausted"
    MOCK SQL "FETCH"
        MOVE 100 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        MOVE 0 TO IP-INTEREST-AMT
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT
    EXPECT WS-ACCTS-PROCESSED TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-FATAL-ERROR-FLAG TO BE "N"
    VERIFY CALL "INTRATE" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> WHEN OTHER: an unexpected DB2 error on FETCH sets FATAL-ERROR-FOUND,
*> which is what stops 2000-PROCESS-ACCOUNTS's loop early.
TESTCASE "2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT sets the fatal-error flag on an unexpected DB2 error"
    MOCK SQL "FETCH"
        MOVE -905 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        MOVE 0 TO IP-INTEREST-AMT
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM 2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT
    EXPECT WS-ACCTS-PROCESSED TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-FATAL-ERROR-FLAG TO BE "Y"
    VERIFY CALL "INTRATE" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

*> Happy path, non-payday: interest accrues into the running total but
*> nothing is paid out yet.
TESTCASE "2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST accrues daily interest on a savings account"
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000001" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
    MOVE 15000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE 2.500000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
    MOVE 10.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE 200.00 TO HV-INTEREST-YTD
    MOVE "20" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
    MOVE 08 TO WS-CURRENT-DAY
    PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED TO BE 11.03
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-YTD TO BE 201.03
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL-ACCRUAL TO BE 1.03
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-INT-PAID-CNT TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED ONCE

*> Edge case: a zero-balance interest-bearing account (e.g. just opened,
*> not yet funded) must accrue zero interest cleanly, not error out.
TESTCASE "2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST accrues zero interest on a zero-balance account"
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000002" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
    MOVE 0.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE 5.000000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
    MOVE 0.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE 0.00 TO HV-INTEREST-YTD
    MOVE "20" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
    MOVE 08 TO WS-CURRENT-DAY
    PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED TO BE 0.00
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-INT-ERRORS TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> Happy path, statement-cycle day: the newly-accrued interest is paid
*> out through 2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT and the running accrual
*> resets to zero.
TESTCASE "2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST posts the accrued interest on the statement cycle day"
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000003" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
    MOVE 15000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE 2.500000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
    MOVE 25.50 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE 300.00 TO HV-INTEREST-YTD
    MOVE "08" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
    MOVE 08 TO WS-CURRENT-DAY
    PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED TO BE 0.00
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-YTD TO BE 301.03
    EXPECT HV-CURRENT-BALANCE TO BE 15026.53
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL-PAID TO BE 26.53
    EXPECT WS-INT-PAID-CNT TO BE 1
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED ONCE

*> Error path -- INTRATE fails. NOTE: the real call site
*> (2100-FETCH-ACCOUNT's "PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST") is missing
*> "THRU 2200-EXIT"; see the bug write-up at the bottom of this file.
*> Testing this branch via the bare, uncorrected call site makes the
*> instrumented program fall through 2200-EXIT into
*> 2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT and then 3000-FINALIZE for real (not just
*> a mocked boundary), which crashes on the never-opened INTRPT file.
*> "THRU 2200-EXIT" here scopes the PERFORM the way the paragraph's own
*> GO TO 2200-EXIT idiom was clearly written to be called, so this test
*> can verify 2200's own early-exit logic without tripping over the
*> caller-side bug it is not this suite's job to work around.
TESTCASE "2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST records an error and skips posting when INTRATE fails"
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        MOVE 8 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000004" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
    MOVE 15000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE 2.500000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
    MOVE 0.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE "99" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
    PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST THRU 2200-EXIT
    EXPECT WS-INT-ERRORS TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Error path -- the DB2 UPDATE of INTEREST_ACCRUED fails after INTRATE
*> succeeds: roll back and record the error, skip the daily-balance
*> insert and the report line. See the note on the previous test case
*> for why this uses "THRU 2200-EXIT".
TESTCASE "2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST rolls back when the DB2 account update fails"
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE -911 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000005" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE "SAV" TO HV-ACCT-TYPE
    MOVE 15000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE 2.500000 TO HV-INTEREST-RATE
    MOVE 0.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE "99" TO HV-STMT-CYCLE
    PERFORM 2200-CALCULATE-INTEREST THRU 2200-EXIT
    EXPECT WS-INT-ERRORS TO BE 1
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 1
    VERIFY SQL "ROLLBACK" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE" WAS CALLED NEVER
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED NEVER

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

TESTCASE "2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT posts a successful interest payment"
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000006" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE 1000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    MOVE "2026-08-08" TO WS-BUSINESS-DATE
    PERFORM 2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT
    EXPECT WS-INT-PAID-CNT TO BE 1
    EXPECT HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED TO BE 0
    EXPECT HV-CURRENT-BALANCE TO BE 1100.00
    EXPECT HV-INT-LAST-PAID TO BE "2026-08-08"
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL-PAID TO BE 100.00
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> The host variables are already mutated locally (balance bumped,
*> accrual zeroed) before the INSERT is attempted, but the DB2 UPDATE
*> that would persist the new balance is only reached when the insert
*> itself succeeds -- so a failed insert leaves the real account row
*> untouched while WS-INT-PAID-CNT never increments.
TESTCASE "2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT records an error and skips the balance update when the insert fails"
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE -803 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOVE "HV000000007" TO HV-ACCT-NUMBER
    MOVE 100.00 TO HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED
    MOVE 1000.00 TO HV-CURRENT-BALANCE
    PERFORM 2300-POST-INTEREST-PAYMENT
    EXPECT WS-INT-PAID-CNT TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-INT-ERRORS TO BE 1
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 2000-PROCESS-ACCOUNTS (multi-account loop)
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

*> A realistic day's run touching three different product tiers (SAV,
*> MMA, CDA) with distinct rates -- proves the cursor loop drives every
*> row through 2100/2200 and stops cleanly at SQLCODE +100.
TESTCASE "2000-PROCESS-ACCOUNTS processes multiple accounts across product tiers"
    MOCK SQL "FETCH" ROWS
        ( HV-ACCT-NUMBER = "HV000000008", HV-ACCT-TYPE = "SAV", HV-CURRENT-BALANCE = 15000.00, HV-INTEREST-RATE = 2.500000, HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED = 0.00, HV-INTEREST-YTD = 0.00, HV-INT-LAST-PAID = "2026-07-01", HV-STMT-CYCLE = "20" )
        ( HV-ACCT-NUMBER = "HV000000009", HV-ACCT-TYPE = "MMA", HV-CURRENT-BALANCE = 50000.00, HV-INTEREST-RATE = 3.750000, HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED = 0.00, HV-INTEREST-YTD = 0.00, HV-INT-LAST-PAID = "2026-07-01", HV-STMT-CYCLE = "21" )
        ( HV-ACCT-NUMBER = "HV000000010", HV-ACCT-TYPE = "CDA", HV-CURRENT-BALANCE = 100000.00, HV-INTEREST-RATE = 4.800000, HV-INTEREST-ACCRUED = 0.00, HV-INTEREST-YTD = 0.00, HV-INT-LAST-PAID = "2026-07-01", HV-STMT-CYCLE = "22" )
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CALL "INTRATE"
        COMPUTE IP-INTEREST-AMT ROUNDED = IP-BALANCE * IP-ANNUAL-RATE / 36500
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "ROLLBACK"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. DAILY_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "INSERT INTO BANK. TRANSACTION_HIST"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET CURRENT_BALANCE"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK WRITE RPT-RECORD
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 08 TO WS-CURRENT-DAY
    PERFORM 2000-PROCESS-ACCOUNTS
    EXPECT WS-ACCTS-PROCESSED TO BE 3
    EXPECT WS-INT-ACCRUED-CNT TO BE 3
    EXPECT WS-TOTAL-ACCRUAL TO BE 19.32
    EXPECT WS-INT-PAID-CNT TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "FETCH" WAS CALLED 4 TIMES
    VERIFY CALL "INTRATE" WAS CALLED 3 TIMES
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE BANK. ACCOUNT SET INTEREST_ACCRUED" WAS CALLED 3 TIMES
    VERIFY WRITE RPT-RECORD WAS CALLED 3 TIMES

*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*> 3000-FINALIZE
*> ---------------------------------------------------------------------

*> NOTE ON ORDERING: this suite compiles to one binary that runs every
*> TESTCASE in sequence, and RETURN-CODE is a single shared COBOL special
*> register that GnuCOBOL also uses as the binary's own process exit
*> code -- so whichever case runs last leaves its RETURN-CODE behind as
*> the whole test binary's exit status. The warning-code case is
*> deliberately placed before the success case (not after) so the suite
*> as a whole still exits 0 when every case passes.
TESTCASE "3000-FINALIZE returns a warning code when interest errors occurred"
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "CLOSE"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE INTRPT
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 3 TO WS-INT-ERRORS
    PERFORM 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 4

TESTCASE "3000-FINALIZE returns success when no interest errors occurred"
    MOCK SQL "COMMIT"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "CLOSE"
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CLOSE INTRPT
    END-MOCK
    MOVE 0 TO WS-INT-ERRORS
    PERFORM 3000-FINALIZE
    EXPECT RETURN-CODE TO BE 0
    VERIFY SQL "COMMIT" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "CLOSE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY CLOSE INTRPT WAS CALLED ONCE
